    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13140" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕ-ŏnĕro</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to unload,
				disburden</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">machinae deoneratae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 24, 6, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, p.
			202</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: ex illius invidia deonerare aliquid
			et in te traicere, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. in
				Caecil. 14, 46</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">foeditate corpora deonerans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, p. 249</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 58, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
